            "review_title": "Review at Coolabah",
            "review_text": "Leean W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam206 contributions\n0\nSurprisingly Delicious\nNov 2020\nWe had heard good recommendations for Coolabah so we decided to try it. At first we were a bit disappointed when we saw it as it is a very small restrobar with just a few tables on one side and the other half being taken up with a bar. There is a pleasant outside seating area although for us most nights in Saigon are too hot to sit outside. We debated whether to stay or not but we are so glad we did. I decided to have the sausages and mash with peas and gravy. I must admit that apart from one restaurant in Ho Chi Minh City I have always been disappointed with the sausage, which are advertised as British bangers, but in fact are no different from the German frankfurters. I actually quite like frankfurters on BBQ's etc. but not when expecting sausages advertised as real British pork sausage. So I half expected the usual suspects from Coolabah. It was a delightful surprise to receive real British tasting pork sausage which were delicious. I had also asked the waitress if the sausage could be well cooked all over and I was happy to see that the sausage were golden brown all over, no pale or uncooked bits , and cooked to perfection. The mash was firm and buttery and very tasty, the peas were the high quality type and not one of the cheap brands where the peas always remain hard and which are sometimes used by other restaurants. The gravy was also delightful. Would we go again? Yes, if only to have that delicious bangers and mash again, although going on the super tasty bangers and mash, we are now also eager to sample their other dishes. The waitress service deserves a mention too as it was first class - very polite, helpful and friendly.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 7, 2021",
